WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:07.282
Jack's mother raced outside with an ax.

2
00:00:07.283 --> 00:00:09.073
"What’s wrong, Jack?"

3
00:00:09.074 --> 00:00:11.668
She looked up and froze.

4
00:00:11.669 --> 00:00:14.648
A pair of legs hung below the clouds.

5
00:00:14.649 --> 00:00:16.847
They were an ogre's legs!

6
00:00:16.848 --> 00:00:22.342
Jack grabbed the ax and swung hard. Chop! Chop!

7
00:00:22.343 --> 00:00:29.904
The ogre growled loudly. "Here I come!"

8
00:00:29.905 --> 00:00:45.403
Jack chopped harder.

9
00:00:45.404 --> 00:00:47.901
A splitting sound filled the air.

10
00:00:47.902 --> 00:00:53.312
The giant beanstalk began to fall.

11
00:00:53.313 --> 00:00:58.680
"Ahh!" The ogre flew off the beanstalk.

12
00:00:58.681 --> 00:01:01.841
Boom! He landed hard on the ground.

13
00:01:01.842 --> 00:01:11.788
Then the beanstalk crashed down.

14
00:01:11.789 --> 00:01:19.562
Under it, the ogre lay still.

15
00:01:19.563 --> 00:01:22.918
Music came from the golden harp.

16
00:01:22.919 --> 00:01:32.770
"You are my new master," it sang.

17
00:01:32.771 --> 00:01:34.813
Mother hugged Jack.

18
00:01:34.814 --> 00:01:37.347
"Thank goodness you're safe!

19
00:01:37.348 --> 00:01:41.983
No more magic beans—or grand plans!"

20
00:01:41.984 --> 00:01:46.683
Jack grinned. "Just one more grand plan."

21
00:01:46.684 --> 00:01:48.869
Mother looked worried.

22
00:01:48.870 --> 00:01:51.951
Jack laughed. "Don't worry!

23
00:01:51.952 --> 00:02:10.092
You'll like this plan—I promise!"

24
00:02:10.093 --> 00:02:16.726
Everyone loved the golden harp.

25
00:02:16.727 --> 00:02:22.525
Jack had concerts and made money.

26
00:02:22.526 --> 00:02:29.355
He gave food to the poor.

27
00:02:29.356 --> 00:02:33.916
And he built a big new house.

28
00:02:33.917 --> 00:02:39.857
Jack built something else too.

29
00:02:39.858 --> 00:02:46.811
One day he knocked on Eliza's door.

30
00:02:46.812 --> 00:02:50.794
"Please come with me," Jack said.

31
00:02:50.795 --> 00:02:54.632
He led her to the field next to his house.

32
00:02:54.633 --> 00:02:59.409
Another new house sat there.

33
00:02:59.410 --> 00:03:07.556
"It's for your family," Jack said.

34
00:03:07.557 --> 00:03:16.499
That night a star twinkled brightly.

35
00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:25.897
And everyone lived happily ever after.

